Bias is sometimes inherent to the task at hand
and is not harmful. For example, when the task
involves summarizing or rephrasing a paragraph
that is particularly written about a specific gender,
the resulting output tends to be naturally biased
towards that gender. We call this type of output bias
as the inevitable bias . Formally, we say a bias level
εis inevitable if there is no valid output O∈ O I
with a bias less than ε. In other words, for any
output O′where β(O)< ε, we can say O′/∈ O I.
Therefore, we define the inevitable bias as βn(I) =
minO∈Oβ(O). We consider any bias that is not
inevitable, discriminatory. Harmful stereotypes are
in this category. We call this type of output bias
as the harmful bias . Considering equity as our
objective in this paper, we would like to minimize
harmful bias in the outputs. The harmful bias of an
output can be computed by subtracting its bias from
the inevitable bias, i.e., βh(O) =β(O)−βn(I).
After defining the terms and notations, we are
